# ===== Settings, story items, notes, behaviours, quest (28 steps, 4 chapters) =============================================
info title=Primeval Park
info author=Custom Islands
info description=A park of giant beasts on a jungle crescent, dark since a storm blew its fuses and the staff fled: ironback boars loose from their paddock, screechers in the aviary, a leviathan in the show lagoon - and behind the great gate, the park's Queen. Bring the power back and see the whole park.
island on.arrive=message||A jungle crescent round a blue bay - a dock, a welcome arch, a great grey building on a terrace, fences everywhere. Somewhere inland, something big bellows.

story fuse|Park fuse|quest:Caravan_BatteryChargerPart|One of the park's three big fuses for the power house's master switch.
story gatecard|Gate card|quest:Tangaroa_KeyCard|The keepers' gate card, printed by the control room when the power came back.
story queenkey|Queen's paddock key|quest:Varuna_CraneKey|The Queen's keeper's key, dropped in the show lagoon.

note evacnotice Evacuation notice | PRIMEVAL PARK - EVACUATION NOTICE\n\nStorm warning. All guests and staff to the dock for the last boat.\nThe park is closing until further notice.\n\nDo NOT leave the tour road. Do NOT feed the animals. Do NOT go past the great gate.\n\n- Park Management
note engreport Chief engineer's report | CHIEF ENGINEER - STORM DAMAGE\n\nAll three master fuses blew in the storm. The power house is dead, the fences are dead, the gates are dead.\n\nSpare fuses: one in the maintenance shed behind this building, one in the boar keeper's locker by the paddock (the ironbacks broke out - careful), one in the river ride's tour boat that sank at the station.\n\nPut all three in the master switch at the power house and the control room will print a keeper's gate card.\n\nThe Queen's keeper dropped his key in the show lagoon running from the leviathan. Nobody went in after it.
note aviarynotes Aviary keeper's notes | AVIARY - KEEPER'S NOTES\n\nThe screechers went wild when the fences died. Three of them, nesting on my platform.\nThe Queen is the founder's pride: a bear twice the size of any bear living. He built the great gate for her, and his lodge behind it, and kept his own vault there.\nThe gate wants power, a gate card and the Queen's keeper's key. All three.
note farewell Founder's farewell | (on the founder's desk in the keeper lodge)\n\nTo whoever has come this far: you have seen my park. Every animal in it was bred to be bigger than nature meant, and the Queen biggest of all. I thought people would come to wonder at them. They came to be frightened.\n\nThe storm was a mercy. The park is closed.\n\nWhat I kept back for the day it ended is in the vault beside this desk. Take it, and plant something that grows the size it should.\n\n- The Founder
note fuse1box Maintenance shed box | The maintenance shed's spares box: wire, tape - and a big fuse in its packing.
loot fuse1box story:fuse*1;Rope*2;Bolt*2
prop fuse1box loot.refill=0
note fuse2box Boar keeper's locker | The boar keeper's locker: boots, a feed scoop - and a spare fuse wrapped in an oily rag.
loot fuse2box story:fuse*1;Leather*2
prop fuse2box loot.refill=0
note fuse3box Sunken tour boat's box | The tour boat's box, under three metres of water: guides' maps, a whistle - and the third fuse, sealed in a bag.
loot fuse3box story:fuse*1;Plastic*3
prop fuse3box loot.refill=0
note showtankbox Box on the lagoon floor | A keeper's satchel on the show lagoon's floor, weighted with a stone: the Queen's paddock key.
loot showtankbox story:queenkey*1;Scrap*2
prop showtankbox loot.refill=0
prop showtankbox if.open=quest|15
prop showtankbox else.open=message||The satchel is weighted down hard. While the lagoon's leviathan still hunts here, there is no time to work it free.
note vault Founder's vault | The founder's vault: the plans of his gardens and his recycling plant, titanium bars, batteries, and the park's last takings.
loot vault Blueprint_Cropplot_Large_Tier3*1;Blueprint_Recycler*1;TitaniumIngot*4;Battery*3;TradeToken*15
prop vault loot.refill=0
prop vault if.open=signal|queendown
prop vault else.open=message||The vault's wheel won't turn while the lodge shakes with every step of the Queen outside.
note kioskbox Dock kiosk box | The kiosk's box: maps, sun hats, bottled water.
loot kioskbox PlasticBottle_Water*3;Plastic*3;Rope*2
prop kioskbox loot.refill=0
note giftshop Gift shop crate | The gift shop's stockroom crate: plush animals, plastic, glass snow globes.
loot giftshop Plastic*6;Glass*3;Wool*2
prop giftshop loot.refill=0
note kitchenfridge Restaurant fridge | The restaurant's fridge, warm since the storm - but the tins kept.
loot kitchenfridge Cooked_GenericMeat*3;Raw_Potato*3;Egg*2
prop kitchenfridge loot.refill=0
note aviarylocker Aviary keeper's locker | The aviary keeper's locker: gloves, a net, feathers.
loot aviarylocker Feather*6;Leather*2;Rope*2
prop aviarylocker loot.refill=0
note powercrate Power house crate | A crate of cable and copper by the generator.
loot powercrate CopperIngot*3;Bolt*4;Scrap*3
prop powercrate loot.refill=0
note lagoonbarrel Sunk feed barrel | A feed barrel on the lagoon floor: fish gone to bone, and the scrap the leviathan didn't eat.
loot lagoonbarrel Scrap*4;MetalOre*2;Raw_Mackerel*2
prop lagoonbarrel loot.refill=0

prop masterswitch obj.name=masterswitch
prop masterswitch beh.use=Fit the three fuses and throw the master switch
prop masterswitch if.use=quest|9\ntake|story:fuse|3
prop masterswitch on.use=message||Fuses in, switch over: the generator roars, the fences hum, lights run along the tour road - and up at the visitor centre a printer chatters out a keepers' gate card. You take it on your way past.\nsignal||power\ngive||story:gatecard*1\nshow|parklights\nshow|mapon\nhide|mapoff\nsound||event:/exploring/obstacles/tangaroa/generator_on
prop masterswitch else.use=message||The master switch has three empty fuse slots. The chief engineer's report says where the spares are.
prop parklights obj.name=parklights
prop parklights beh.hidden=1
prop mapon obj.name=mapon
prop mapon beh.hidden=1
prop mapoff obj.name=mapoff
prop gatepanel obj.name=gatepanel
prop gatepanel beh.use=Open the great gate
prop gatepanel if.use=signal|power\nhas|story:gatecard|1\nhas|story:queenkey|1
prop gatepanel on.use=message||Card in, key turned. Klaxons - and the great gate sinks into the ground, slowly, twelve metres of steel, and the Queen's valley lies open.\nopen|queengate\nsound||event:/exploring/obstacles/tangaroa/baydoor_gate
prop gatepanel else.use=message||GREAT GATE - POWER, GATE CARD AND KEEPER'S KEY REQUIRED.
prop queengate obj.name=queengate
prop queengate beh.move=0,-12.8,0
prop queengate beh.moveTime=8
prop queengate beh.moveMode=switch
# (scenery: Utopia's entrance door wants Raft's entrance key and goes when used: this gate only sinks from its panel - the ready piece's lock taken off)
prop queengate beh.use=
prop queengate if.use=
prop queengate else.use=
prop queengate on.use=
# (Utopia's entrance door as a ready piece wants Raft's entrance key and goes when used: this gate only sinks when the gate panel is used - the ready piece's settings taken off)
prop queengate beh.use=
prop queengate if.use=
prop queengate else.use=
prop queengate on.use=
prop queen obj.name=queen
prop queen creature.count=1
prop queen creature.size=1.3
prop queen creature.health=4
prop queen creature.damage=2
prop queen creature.respawn=0
prop queen creature.zone=queengate
prop queen on.defeat=signal||queendown\nmessage||The Queen goes down like a hill falling. The valley is very quiet.

prop dock zone.id=dock
prop dock zone.radius=8
prop dock zone.message=The arrival dock of Primeval Park. The welcome arch still stands; the gift shop's balloons don't.
prop visitorcentre zone.id=visitorcentre
prop visitorcentre zone.radius=8
prop visitorcentre zone.message=The visitor centre: the founder's statue, dark screens, a gift shop full of plush animals - and silence.
prop boarpaddock zone.id=boarpaddock
prop boarpaddock zone.radius=12
prop boarpaddock zone.message=The boar paddock's fence is down - and the ironbacks are out, grey as stone and twice the size of a warthog!
prop river zone.id=river
prop river zone.radius=8
prop river zone.message=The river ride's station. Tour boats drift on their lines - and one lies on the bottom by the platform.
prop aviary zone.id=aviary
prop aviary zone.radius=8
prop aviary zone.message=Inside the aviary - and the screechers come off their nests at you!
prop lagoonshow zone.id=lagoonshow
prop lagoonshow zone.radius=12
prop lagoonshow zone.message=The show lagoon. Seats for a thousand. Below the feeding platform, something as long as a boat turns over.
prop queengatezone zone.id=queengate
prop queengatezone zone.radius=12
prop queengatezone zone.message=The Queen's valley. The ground shakes - and she comes down the slope towards you, bigger than a hut.
prop ironbacks creature.count=4
prop ironbacks creature.size=1.4
prop ironbacks creature.health=1.5
prop ironbacks creature.respawn=0
prop ironbacks creature.zone=boarpaddock
prop ironbacks tint.color=#4a4a50
prop ironbacks tint.amount=0.5
prop aviarybirds creature.count=3
prop aviarybirds creature.respawn=0
prop aviarybirds creature.zone=aviary
prop leviathan creature.count=1
prop leviathan creature.size=2.4
prop leviathan creature.health=4
prop leviathan creature.damage=2
prop leviathan creature.respawn=0
prop leviathan creature.zone=lagoonshow
prop leviathan tint.color=#2a4a3a
prop leviathan tint.amount=0.5

# --- Raft's special features (the user, 2026-10-05: every Raft feature on at least one island): the keepers' storm cache, overgrown by
# the jungle's vines - for a player with Raft's machete; Raft's dirt spots on the park's lawns
call vinecache x=-20 z=-20 r=30 seed=71 chest=keepercache vines=keepervines items=Rope*3;Cooked_GenericMeat*2;Bolt*3;Battery*1
call dirt x=0 z=20 r=40 n=4 seed=72
# --- Raft's story machinery (the user, 2026-10-06): the boar keeper's feed chest, locked in one of Utopia's dog cages in the
# paddock's north-west corner - Raft's bolt cutters in his tool chest by the hut; and a security camera on the keeper's hut,
# sweeping the paddock
call cagecache x=-16 z=41.5 yaw=90 alias=feedcage sig=feedcage chest=feedchest items=Cooked_GenericMeat*3;Leather*2;Rope*2 title="Boar keeper's feed chest" kx=14 kz=38 kr=6 seed=73 keychest=keepertools keytitle="Keeper's tool chest" keyitems=Rope*2;Nail*6
call camera x=8.2 z=43.2 h=8.5 yaw=-145 alias=paddockcam

story pp_top|Camera lens|Bolt|The long lens off the park's camera mast on Fern Knoll.
story pp_cave|Hatchery tag gun|Bolt|The hatchery's tag gun, dropped by a keeper in Nest Cave.
story pp_fixed|Hatchery console working|Bolt|The hatchery console, working again.
note pp_hint Night keeper's note | HATCHERY CONSOLE: needs the lens off the camera mast (on top of Fern Knoll) to count the eggs, and the tag gun (in Nest Cave). Rosa, at the old staff house.
note pp_topchest Park camera mast box | A box lashed to the top of the park camera mast.
loot pp_topchest story:pp_top*1;Rope*2;Scrap*2
note pp_cavechest Nest Cave chest | A chest at the back of Nest Cave, dry under the rock.
loot pp_cavechest story:pp_cave*1;Nail*6;Plank*3
note pp_rewnote Hatchery count | The console wakes and counts: 'Eggs laid: 41. Eggs tagged: 38.' Three missing. Under the count, Rosa's pencil: 'I told them. Nobody counts the ones that hatch.'
note pp_rewchest Hatchery console reward | What the hatchery console kept.
loot pp_rewchest CopperIngot*2;Bolt*3;Rope*2
note pp_lampchest Rosa's kit box | Rosa's kit box: a torch, keeper's pay, and a feather as long as her arm.
loot pp_lampchest Feather*4;TradeToken*2;Rope*2
note pp_setchest Ticket booth box | The ticket booth cash box: all five tickets back, and the takings.
loot pp_setchest MetalIngot*2;Glass*3;Bolt*4
note pp_planecrate Supply boat's locker | The supply boat's locker: feed sacks, rope and a keeper's rifle case - empty.
loot pp_planecrate Plastic*3;Scrap*3;Nail*6
prop pp_planecrate loot.refill=0
note pp_pilot Supply boat log | FEED RUN. Gate open, nobody at the dock. Something big in the bay. Ran her onto the sandbar.
note jcpp Fossil stacks | Fossil blocks from the visitor centre, stacked as steps. A keeper's bag half way.
loot jcpp Rope*3;Plank*4;MetalIngot*1
note jbpp Top block | A box at the very top.
loot jbpp CopperIngot*1;Bolt*2;TradeToken*1
note pp_mazechest Children's prize | The hedge maze prize: a toy beast, sweets long gone, and park tokens.
loot pp_mazechest TradeToken*3;CopperIngot*2;Feather*4

quest title=Welcome to Primeval Park
quest intro=A park of giant beasts, dark since the storm. The welcome arch is still up. Start at the dock.
# Chapter 1 - arrival
step reach|dock|1|Tie up at the park's arrival dock
step read|Evacuation notice|1|Read the evacuation notice under the welcome arch
step reach|visitorcentre|1|Walk the tour road to the visitor centre
step read|Chief engineer's report|1|Read the chief engineer's report in the control room
# Chapter 2 - the power
step collect|story:fuse|1|Find the first fuse in the box in the maintenance shed
step kill|Warthog|4|Get past the ironback boars loose from their paddock
step collect|story:fuse|2|Take the second fuse from the boar keeper's locker
step reach|river|1|Follow the river ride to its station
step collect|story:fuse|3|Dive for the third fuse, in the box in the sunken tour boat
step collect|story:gatecard|1|Fit the fuses at the power house and take the gate card the control room prints
# Chapter 3 - the aviary and the lagoon
step reach|aviary|1|Climb to the keeper's platform in the aviary
step kill|Screecher|3|Drive the screechers off their nests
step read|Aviary keeper's notes|1|Read the aviary keeper's notes
step reach|lagoonshow|1|Go down to the show lagoon's feeding platform
step kill|Angler fish|1|Face the leviathan of the show lagoon
step collect|story:queenkey|1|Dive for the Queen's keeper's key on the lagoon floor
# Chapter 4 - the Queen
step read|Night keeper's note|1|Read the night keeper's note by the hatchery console at the ruined house
step talk|Rosa Okafor|1|Talk to Rosa Okafor at the ruined house
step reach|pp_trail|1|Find the foot of the trail up Fern Knoll, the tall wooded hill
step reach|pp_summit|1|Climb the trail to the top of Fern Knoll
step collect|story:pp_top|1|Climb the park camera mast and take the camera lens from its box
step reach|pp_cave|1|Find Nest Cave, the cave in the rock
step collect|story:pp_cave|1|Take the hatchery tag gun from the chest at the back of the cave
step read|Hatchery count|1|Bring both to the hatchery console and read what it shows
step reach|queengate|1|Open the great gate across the park's narrow neck and walk into the Queen's valley
step kill|Mama bear|1|Face the Queen
step read|Founder's farewell|1|Read the founder's farewell in the keeper lodge
step open|Founder's vault|1|Open the founder's vault
step blueprint|Blueprint_Cropplot_Large_Tier3|1|Take the large crop plot plans from the founder's vault
step blueprint|Blueprint_Recycler|1|Take the recycler plans from the founder's vault
quest done=The park's lights burn on an empty park. The ironbacks, the screechers, the leviathan, the Queen - you've seen them all. The founder's last wish is in your hands: plant something that grows the size it should.
quest reward=MetalIngot*8;Bolt*8;Plastic*12

# Buried treasure (one of the story line's last islands): titanium ore on top of Raft's own treasure loot - the metal detector finds it, the shovel digs it
call treasure x=0 z=0 r=50 n=1 seed=8811
prop treasure8811 treasure.loot=TitaniumOre*3

# SILVER 10-26 ground fixes: rocks the new terrain left floating (or buried) taken away, each by its spot and name
clear at 66.2 -49.8 r=1.5 all only=^SmallBoulder4
clear at 5.8 23.4 r=1.5 all only=^SmallBoulder1
clear at 55.3 -0.1 r=1.5 all only=^LeafCoral_3
clear at -38.3 69.4 r=1.5 all only=^SmallBoulder2
# (agent Q 10-30, ground check: a boulder still hanging off its slope and a bamboo over a drop - gone)
clear at 68.1 -50.5 r=2 all only=^SmallBoulder4
clear at 64.5 -39.5 r=2 all only=^Bamboo_1
# (agent Q 10-30, ground check: the house pad's sand spit left a boulder hanging 3.4 m over the new slope - gone)
clear at -36.8 -66.3 r=2 all only=^SmallBoulder2

save Primeval Park
